{
  "chapter": "workflows/the-determinism-test",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Three questions about a piece of work, answered before any code is written:",
    "  stepsKnownUpfront  — do you know what has to happen?",
    "  branchesEnumerable — can you list every decision point and its options?",
    "  needsJudgement     — does some step require reading unstructured input?",
    "The first two decide the shape. The third only decides whether a model appears inside it."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "fully-deterministic-work-is-a-workflow",
      "signals": { "stepsKnownUpfront": true, "branchesEnumerable": true, "needsJudgement": false },
      "verdict": "workflow"
    },
    {
      "id": "needing-a-model-does-not-make-it-an-agent",
      "signals": { "stepsKnownUpfront": true, "branchesEnumerable": true, "needsJudgement": true },
      "verdict": "workflow-with-model-steps"
    },
    {
      "id": "unknown-steps-make-it-an-agent",
      "signals": { "stepsKnownUpfront": false, "branchesEnumerable": true, "needsJudgement": false },
      "verdict": "agent"
    },
    {
      "id": "unenumerable-branches-make-it-an-agent",
      "signals": { "stepsKnownUpfront": true, "branchesEnumerable": false, "needsJudgement": false },
      "verdict": "agent"
    },
    {
      "id": "unknown-structure-outranks-the-judgement-question",
      "signals": { "stepsKnownUpfront": false, "branchesEnumerable": true, "needsJudgement": true },
